---
import data from '../data/foundation-results.json';
const {kind}=Astro.props as {kind:'generation'|'representations'|'playlists'|'transformer'|'cache'};
const generation=data.generation, cache=data.cache;
const average=(values:number[])=>values.reduce((sum,value)=>sum+value,0)/values.length;
---
{kind==='generation' && <div class="reference-brief"><h3>Actual generated continuation</h3><p><strong>Prompt:</strong> {generation.prompt}</p><p><strong>New text:</strong> <code>{JSON.stringify(generation.continuation)}</code></p><p>The repeated “sun” is an observed failure of this small base model. It is retained rather than replaced with a polished example.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Input IDs</th><td>{generation.input_ids.join(', ')}</td></tr><tr><th>Embedding table</th><td>{generation.embedding_shape.join(' × ')}</td></tr><tr><th>Final states</th><td>{generation.hidden_shape.join(' × ')}</td></tr><tr><th>LM logits</th><td>{generation.logits_shape.join(' × ')}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>}
{kind==='transformer' && <div class="reference-brief"><h3>Transparent random-weight trace</h3><p>Inputs: [{data.transformer.input_shape.join(', ')}] · Q/K/V per-head layout: [{data.transformer.qkv_shape.join(', ')}] · vocabulary logits: [{data.transformer.head_shape.join(', ')}].</p><p>Maximum difference from PyTorch attention: {data.transformer.reference_max_error.toExponential(3)}. Future weights are exactly zero. This verifies the calculation, not language ability.</p><p>Last-position toy logits: {data.transformer.logits.map(x=>x.toFixed(3)).join(', ')}.</p></div>}
{kind==='cache' && <div class="reference-brief"><h3>Correctness before speed</h3><p>Recorded precision: {cache.dtype}. Maximum cached/uncached logit difference: {cache.max_logit_error.toExponential(3)}. Cache K/V shape per layer: [{cache.cache_shape.join(', ')}], across {cache.layers} layers. Actual K/V tensors occupy {cache.cache_bytes.toLocaleString()} bytes.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Same forced continuation</th><th>Mean warmed CPU time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Uncached</td><td>{average(cache.cpu_seconds.uncached).toFixed(5)} s</td></tr><tr><td>Cached</td><td>{average(cache.cpu_seconds.cached).toFixed(5)} s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>{cache.measurement} Timings include prefill; these short float64 runs are not a production benchmark or GPU speed claim.</p></div>}
{kind==='playlists' && <div class="reference-brief"><h3>Fixed held-out comparison</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Recall@3</th><th>MRR</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Learned vectors</td><td>{data.playlists.test.recall_at_3.toFixed(3)}</td><td>{data.playlists.test.mrr.toFixed(3)}</td></tr><tr><td>Train-only popularity</td><td>{data.playlists.test.popularity_recall_at_3.toFixed(3)}</td><td>{data.playlists.test.popularity_mrr.toFixed(3)}</td></tr></tbody></table><p>{data.playlists.test.queries} test queries, {data.playlists.trained_pairs} training center/context pairs, {data.playlists.item_count} fitted items. Some targets miss the top three. These synthetic themes are deliberately narrow; the result does not measure real listening preference.</p></div>}
{kind==='representations' && <p class="quiet-note">GloVe artifact: {data.representations.static_shape[0].toLocaleString()} × {data.representations.static_shape[1]}. The artifact SHA-256, model revisions, exact pooling, and numeric results are in the run record/source. Do not mix these 50D word rows with 128D token states or 384D sentence embeddings as if their coordinates were compatible.</p>}
